      <h>469</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Additional constraints
--

- Publication: A project cannot be 
published (draftMode = false) unless 
it has at least one invention.

- Cascade Publishing: Publishing a 
project automatically publishes all of its 
components (inventions, campaigns, 
and strategies).

- Draft Components: Project members 
can add components (inventions, 
campaigns, strategies) to a project even 
if those components are still in 
draft mode.

- Visibility: Every member of a project 
can display all data/components 
involved in that project, even if they are 
not published yet.

- Effort Calculation (PMs): The / effort of 
a project is computed as the sum of 
active months of all its components 
(inventions, campaigns, strategies) 
divided by the total number of people 
involved (inventors + spokespeople + fundraisers).

- Sponsorships and Audits: Sponsors 
and auditors can only attach their 
Sponsorships or AuditReports to a 
project if BOTH the project and the 
attached document are published.

- Date Interval: kickOff / closeOut must be a valid 
time interval in the future with respect to the 
moment when a project is published.

bg=RED
</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
